            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/Utils.hpp",
                    "line": 310,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Follow-up on the std::move comment \u2014 would you consider taking this one step further and extracting a private helper that operates on the already-prefixed interfaces? Something like:\n```\nvoid getConfiguration(std::span<const std::string_view> types, size_t retries = 0)\n{\n    std::vector<std::string> interfaces;\n    interfaces.reserve(types.size());\n    for (const auto& type : types)\n        interfaces.push_back(configInterfaceName(type));\n        getConfigurationImpl(std::move(interfaces), retries);\n}\n\nprivate:\nvoid getConfigurationImpl(std::vector<std::string> interfaces, size_t retries);\n```\nThen the retry just does self->getConfigurationImpl(std::move(interfaces), retries - 1); \u2014 no typesCopy, no string_view round-trip, and the double-prefix bug becomes structurally impossible since the prefix is only ever applied in the public entry. The current fix works but the API shape that caused the bug is still there."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/Utils.hpp",
                    "line": 310,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, thanks for review."
                },
                {
